# Data Availability and Use

This repository contains source code developed for research on residual chlorine forecasting and model generalizability across water treatment plants. The datasets used in the study are not distributed through this public repository.

The study used operational data from three water treatment plants:

1. Alexander Orr Water Treatment Plant
2. Sergio Cuevas Water Treatment Plant
3. Los Filtros Water Treatment Plant

The MIT License included in this repository applies only to the original source code and notebook materials created by the repository author. It does not apply to the underlying water treatment plant datasets, third-party materials, or data supplied by external organizations.

The Alexander Orr operational dataset is not included in this repository. Access and reuse are subject to authorization and the data-governance requirements of the data provider.

The Sergio Cuevas and Los Filtros datasets were externally provided for this research. No public redistribution authorization was provided; therefore, these datasets are not included in this repository. They may not be copied, redistributed, published, or used for other purposes without authorization from their respective data providers.

Anyone seeking access to these datasets must contact the respective data owners or providers directly. Availability is subject to provider approval and any applicable confidentiality, security, institutional, or data-use restrictions.

The repository code may be reused under the MIT License. Users must provide their own appropriately authorized data and configure the necessary file paths and column mappings.
